Subject: [PATCH] interconnect: qcom: sm8550: mark bcm_lp0 keepalive

On Samsung Galaxy Tab S9 (gts9wifi), the bootloader leaves a non-zero
APPS RSC vote on LP0 (bcm_lp0, owned exclusively by lpass_lpiaon_noc).
Because Linux currently has no interconnect consumer voting on bcm_lp0,
enabling lpass_lpiaon_noc with keepalive=false causes sync_state() to
flush LP0 to 0 in ACTIVE (AMC), WAKE and SLEEP ~15-30s after boot,
crashing the running LPASS/ADSP and triggering an immediate hard SoC
reset.  Conversely, keeping lpass_lpiaon_noc disabled leaves LP0 out of
the RPMh [sleep] TCS permanently, keeping the bootloader's LP0 vote
active across suspend.

Mark bcm_lp0 keepalive = true (matching bcm_mc0 / bcm_cn0 / bcm_sh0) so
bcm-voter maintains a minimum floor vote (1) in AMC and WAKE while
flushing LP0 to 0 in the SLEEP TCS during system suspend.

---
--- a/drivers/interconnect/qcom/sm8550.c
+++ b/drivers/interconnect/qcom/sm8550.c
@@ -1123,6 +1123,7 @@
 
 static struct qcom_icc_bcm bcm_lp0 = {
 	.name = "LP0",
+	.keepalive = true,
 	.num_nodes = 2,
 	.nodes = { &qnm_lpass_lpinoc, &qns_lpass_aggnoc },
 };
